ication of Diseases, 9th Revision, Clinical Modification (ICD-9-CM)</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>DHHS Publication No. (PHS) 80&#x02013;1260</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ellekjaer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kruger</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Terent</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of incident stroke in Norway: hospital discharge data compared with a population-based stroke register</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>1999</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9880388</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reker</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosen</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoenig</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Berlowitz</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Laughlin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Marshall</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rittman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The hazards of stroke case selection using administrative data</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>2002</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>96</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11802082</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005650-200202000-00004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tirschwell</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Longstr